    "description": "Original MCQs for a German supply-chain due-diligence compliance-training module on the Lieferkettensorgfaltspflichtengesetz (LkSG), covering the scope of application and employee thresholds (Sec. 1 LkSG, currently 1,000 domestic employees since 1 Jan 2024, previously 3,000 since 1 Jan 2023, including group/Konzern attribution under Sec. 1(3)), the core due diligence duties and risk analysis (Sec. 3-5 LkSG), preventive and remedial measures including the distinct rules for the company's own business area vs. direct vs. indirect suppliers (Sec. 6, 7, 9 LkSG), the grievance mechanism (Sec. 8 LkSG), and administrative fines/enforcement by BAFA including the turnover-based fine for companies above EUR 400 million average annual turnover and the public-procurement exclusion (Sec. 19, 22, 24 LkSG). Also flags the pending 2025/2026 government bill to abolish the Sec. 10 reporting duty and narrow the fine catalogue (cabinet-approved September 2025, still in Bundestag committee as of early 2026, not yet in force as of this module's writing) so learners aren't misled about which rules currently apply. Content is independently phrased and grounded directly in LkSG statute text (gesetze-im-internet.de mirror) and BAFA guidance, NOT sourced or paraphrased from any commercial compliance-training vendor's catalog. This is a fully independent exam module - separate content pool, separate exam simulation from every other module.",
    "class": "ALL",
    "canonical_locale": "de",
    "point_system": "2-4 points per question, matching this app's existing style",
    "pass_rule_note": "Launched directly as a 30-question pool (6 per topic), sized for a corporate compliance knowledge-check rather than a driving-exam-length test, same DN-54 pattern already used for kyc_aml/kartellrecht. Exam Simulation/Training draws 6 questions per run (one topic gets 2, the other four get 1 each), max 4 error points to pass, auto-fail on 2+ wrong high_stakes questions, 10-minute time limit in Simulation mode. See app/app.js's EXAM_QUESTION_COUNT_BY_TYPE / MAX_ERROR_POINTS_BY_TYPE / EXAM_TIME_LIMIT_MS_BY_TYPE / EXAM_TOPIC_DRAW.",
